Relevant columns, their potential usage and likely conditions  

• PUBLICATIONS."family_id": family identifier – GROUP BY / COUNT; exclude rows where "family_id" = '-1'.  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": unique publication id – JOIN key to ABS_AND_EMB."publication_number".  
• ABS_AND_EMB."publication_number": JOIN key coming from PUBLICATIONS."publication_number".  
• ABS_AND_EMB."abstract": text of the abstract – filter out NULL or empty values (TRIM("abstract") <> '').  

Typical filter / join conditions that will be needed  

1. PUBLICATIONS."family_id" <> '-1'  
2. ABS_AND_EMB."abstract" IS NOT NULL AND TRIM(ABS_AND_EMB."abstract") <> ''  
3. PUBLICATIONS."publication_number" = ABS_AND_EMB."publication_number"  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each different, all limited to 20 rows).  
They go from very simple inspections to a final query that fulfils the task requirement.  
Every column name is wrapped in double quotes and the fully qualified table name is used.

```sql
-- Description: Peek at distinct family_id values that are not '-1'
SELECT DISTINCT "family_id"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "family_id" <> '-1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Sample publication numbers together with their family IDs
SELECT "publication_number",
       "family_id"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "family_id" <> '-1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Count publications per family to see which families are large
SELECT "family_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "pub_cnt"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "family_id" <> '-1'
GROUP BY "family_id"
ORDER BY "pub_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Inspect a handful of abstracts and their publication numbers
SELECT "publication_number",
       "abstract"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB
WHERE "abstract" IS NOT NULL
  AND TRIM("abstract") <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Join publications with abstracts, show 20 sample joined rows
SELECT p."publication_number",
       p."family_id",
       a."abstract"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS  AS p
JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB   AS a
  ON p."publication_number" = a."publication_number"
WHERE p."family_id" <> '-1'
  AND a."abstract" IS NOT NULL
  AND TRIM(a."abstract") <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Compute publication counts per family using the joined dataset
SELECT p."family_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "pub_with_abs_cnt"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS  AS p
JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB   AS a
  ON p."publication_number" = a."publication_number"
WHERE p."family_id" <> '-1'
  AND a."abstract" IS NOT NULL
  AND TRIM(a."abstract") <> ''
GROUP BY p."family_id"
ORDER BY "pub_with_abs_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Identify the top‑6 families (by total publications) – sub‑query method
SELECT "family_id"
FROM (
    SELECT "family_id",
           COUNT(*) AS "pub_cnt"
    FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
    WHERE "family_id" <> '-1'
    GROUP BY "family_id"
    ORDER BY "pub_cnt" DESC
    LIMIT 6
) AS top6
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Pull every publication for the previously computed top‑6 families
WITH top6 AS (
    SELECT "family_id"
    FROM (
        SELECT "family_id",
               COUNT(*) AS "pub_cnt"
        FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
        WHERE "family_id" <> '-1'
        GROUP BY "family_id"
        ORDER BY "pub_cnt" DESC
        LIMIT 6
    )
)
SELECT p."family_id",
       p."publication_number"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS p
JOIN top6 t
  ON p."family_id" = t."family_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
